{"text": "is POLK awarow\u00ae\n\n450 LEXINGTON AVENUE\n\nNew York, N.Y, 10017\n\nNovember 11, 1999\n\nMemorandum for: Charles A. Blixt, Esq\nMartin J, Barrington, Esq\nNeil E. Mellen, Esq.\nJames A. Wilson, Esq,\n\nRe: Compensation of Fee Panel Arbitrators\n\nEnclosed with this memorandum is a schedule of amounts due to be paid\nto members of the fee arbitration panel. We have received (i) three invoices from\nChairman John Calhoun Wells covering the Massachusetts, Hawaii and Ilinois\narbitrations, (ji) an invoice from Judge Renfrew with respect to the month of\nSeptember, (ii) an invoice from Harry Huge with respect to the Hawaii\narbitration, (iv) an invoice from Jack F. Dunbar with respect to the Ulinois\narbitration and (v) an invoice from Shearman & Sterling, counsel to the arbitration\npanel, for services rendered during the month of September, 1999\n\nThe accompanying schedule shows each company's share of the each\npayment, based on 1998 Relative Market Shares as computed pursuant to the\nMSA. Esch company should ensure that calculations of the payments are correct.\n\u2018The invoices that we have received from the arbitrators and their legal counsel,\nwhich detail the amounts of fees and compensable expenses, are enclosed as well\n\nCharles Duggan\n\nEnclosures\nce w/ene: Stephen J. Krigbaum, Esq\nce wlo enc: Meyer G. Koplow, Esq.\nRonald S. Milstein, Esq.\nStephen R. Patton, Esq\n\nBy Overnight Courier or\n\nby Hand (in New York City\n\nLOLSHSSS", "words": [{"text": "is", "x0": 239, "y0": 91, "x1": 298, "y1": 116, "conf": 42.0}, {"text": "POLK", "x0": 310, "y0": 106, "x1": 361, "y1": 116, "conf": 94.0}, {"text": "awarow\u00ae", "x0": 371, "y0": 91, "x1": 497, "y1": 118, "conf": 31.0}, {"text": "450", "x0": 291, "y0": 143, "x1": 321, "y1": 151, "conf": 85.0}, {"text": "LEXINGTON", "x0": 331, "y0": 144, "x1": 401, "y1": 151, "conf": 68.0}, {"text": "AVENUE", "x0": 410, "y0": 144, "x1": 462, "y1": 152, "conf": 37.0}, {"text": "New", "x0": 296, "y0": 160, "x